{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count of satisfying assignments for CNF with 12 variables. Clauses list. Let's enumerate? 12 variables, 12 clauses. Could use brute force? 2^12=4096 manageable. But we can reason maybe. Let's attempt manual deduction.\n\nClauses:\n\n1. (-3 OR 8)\n2. (11 OR 9)\n3. (-4 OR 12)\n4. (-10 OR 8)\n5. (10 OR 3)\n6. (-9 OR 7)\n7. (-5 OR 2)\n8. (5 OR 6)\n9. (-11 OR 7)\n10. (-1 OR 12)\n11. (-6 OR 2)\n12. (1 OR 4)\n\nWe need assignments satisfying all.\n\nLet's analyze constraints.\n\nFrom clause 12: (1 OR 4) => at least one of x1 or x4 true.\n\nClause 10: (-1 OR 12) => not x1 or x12 true. Equivalent: x1 -> x12. So if x1 true then x12 true. If x1 false, clause satisfied regardless of x12.\n\nClause 3: (-4 OR 12) => not x4 or x12 true. So x4 -> x12.\n\nClause 1: (-3 OR 8) => not x3 or x8 true. So x3 -> x8.\n\nClause 4: (-10 OR 8) => not x10 or x8 true. So x10 -> x8.\n\nClause 5: (10 OR 3) => x10 or x3 true. So at least one of x10, x3 true.\n\nClause 2: (11 OR 9) => x11 or x9 true.\n\nClause 6: (-9 OR 7) => not x9 or x7 true. So x9 -> x7.\n\nClause 9: (-11 OR 7) => not x11 or x7 true. So x11 -> x7.\n\nClause 7: (-5 OR 2) => not x5 or x2 true. So x5 -> x2.\n\nClause 8: (5 OR 6) => x5 or x6 true.\n\nClause 11: (-6 OR 2) => not x6 or x2 true. So x6 -> x2.\n\nThus x5 or x6 true, and both imply x2. So x2 must be true if either x5 or x6 true. But clause 7 and 11 ensure that if x5 true then x2 true; if x6 true then x2 true. However x2 could be true even if both false? No clause forces x2 true except from these implications. But there is no clause requiring x2 true unless x5 or x6 true. So x2 can be false if both x5 and x6 false.\n\nBut clause 7 and 11 are implications; they don't require antecedent. So x5 false, x6 false allowed.\n\nNow consider x3, x10, x8.\n\nClause 5: x10 or x3 true. So at least one of them true.\n\nClause 1: x3 -> x8. Clause 4: x10 -> x8. So if either x3 or x10 true, then x8 must be true. So x8 true if at least one of x3,x10 true. But clause 1 and 4 also allow x8 true even if both false? Clause 1: (-3 OR 8) satisfied if x8 true regardless of x3. Clause 4: (-10 OR 8) satisfied if x8 true regardless of x10. So x8 can be true independent"}}],"created":1790937423,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":3797,"total_tokens":4565,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-Ov1e109SXp7QYnjowjQhWhnAkSQ73A30","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":3797,"prompt_ms":485.78,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.12793784566763233,"prompt_per_second":7816.295442381325,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2480.281,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.2337431551499347,"predicted_per_second":309.23915475706184}}